## Free-form structured summary (extracted from paper.txt)

- **Design:** 4 doses (0, 0.1, 0.25, 1.0 Gy) × 2 timepoints (10 d, 30 d) × 10 C57BL/6J mice = 80 fecal pellets. Radiation: $^{16}$O ions, 600 MeV/n, at NASA Space Radiation Laboratory (NSRL), whole-body.
- **Assays:** 16S V4 amplicon (F515/R806) on Illumina HiSeq 2500 (paired 101 bp); untargeted UPLC-Q-TOF LC-MS on the same fecal aliquots.
- **Deposits (as stated in paper):** SRA SRP098151 (16S) — confirmed live and downloadable. LC-MS: "will be made available on Dryad" — **NO Dryad DOI/handle provided in text** (reproducibility blocker for the metabolomics arm).
- **Analytical arms:** (1) 16S ecology (~50% of paper), (2) PICRUSt+FishTaco functional shifts (~20%), (3) LC-MS metabolomics + CMP metabolic-network modelling (~30%).
- **Central finding:** low-dose (0.1 Gy) $^{16}$O drives a dramatic *Akkermansia muciniphila* / Verrucomicrobia bloom (paper: ~18% vs <1% controls; our re-derivation: 17.28% vs 0.50%, MWU p=0.001), a non-monotonic Dose × Time interaction, and a hormetic/HRS-IRR pattern where 1 Gy has weaker community-level effect at 30 d than 0.1–0.25 Gy.
